Use a wrapper struct that contains the original struct as a private field and exposes new methods. For example:

```rust
struct BaseData {
    value: i32,
}

struct ExtendedData {
    base: BaseData,
    // Private extension fields
    cached_result: Option<i32>,
}

impl ExtendedData {
    fn new(value: i32) -> Self {
        Self {
            base: BaseData { value },
            cached_result: None,
        }
    }

    fn get_computed_value(&mut self) -> i32 {
        if let Some(cached) = self.cached_result {
            cached
        } else {
            let result = self.base.value * 2;
            self.cached_result = Some(result);
            result
        }
    }
}
```

This pattern keeps the base struct's fields private while adding new functionality.

